  "replay_prefix": "GORDIAN_TRIG",
  "outcomes": [
    1,
    2
  ],
  "instructions": "This is a reduced FDLibM j0 guard with actual linked sine/cosine implementations. Use sin(x)*cos(x)=sin(2*x)/2 to derive safe sign intervals. Return 1 for a negative product and 2 for a nonnegative product. Headers stdint.h, string.h and klee/klee.h are already provided. Positive finite binary64 encodings sort as unsigned integers. Avoid trigonometric zeros and rounding boundaries when restricting the domain."
}
